		{"id":"uncertainty","type":"text","text":"### Uncertainty\n\n- Abstract-only sources keep their limit\n- Effect sizes are population averages\n- Reviews inherit the biases of their studies","x":0,"y":609,"width":460,"height":154,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"hypothesis","type":"text","text":"### Open questions\n\n- What design would let a claim about a mechanism be tested rather than merely observed?\n- Which confounders can be measured, and which only randomised assignment can balance?\n- How far can a result travel before the population no longer matches?","x":0,"y":823,"width":460,"height":232,"color":"6"},
